.TH PSDotProduct 3 2023-12-07 "PsyC 0.9.3" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
PSDotProduct

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/maths.h>

.I
PSFloat  
.br
\fBPSDotProduct\fR(\fIPSFloat *a\fR, \fIPSFloat *b\fR, \fIuint64_t length\fR, \fIPSMathOpts *opts\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compute the dot product of vector \fIa\fR and vector \fIb\fR, both having length defined by \fIlength\fR.
.br
The dot product is the sum of the product of each element of \fIa\fR by the corresponding element of \fIb\fR at the same index (`a[0] * b[0] + a[1] * b[1] + ... + a[n] * b[n]`).
.br
The function can take advantage of the available accelerations (both hardwware and software). By default, accelerations set in \fIPSGlobalAcceleration\fR are used, if any. However, the used accelerations methods can be changed via the \fIacceleration\fR member of the optional argument \fIopts\fR.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The resulting dot product (scalar) or zero if \fIa\fR is \fINULL\fR or \fIb\fR is \fINULL\fR.
